{
  "$comment": "What the launcher's documents are held to: a knowledge base's, the stack's kinds (KnowledgeBase, KnowledgeIndex, Inference) and the project file `.semiont/config.yaml` (ProjectConfig, in ../kb-identity); and the shared ones, the Browser's (Browser), the worker's (WorkerPool), the issuer's (Issuer) and the vector store's (VectorStore), which belong to no knowledge base. Each case names the schema it is read against and gives the document: `document`, YAML text, where YAML's own reading is the point or no fixture holds the kind; or `base`, a file of the launcher's fixtures (its fixture knowledge base, and the state home's documents beside it), with `patch`, a JSON merge patch (RFC 7396) applied to it. `verdict` is `accepted`, or `refused` with `at`, the JSON pointer of the value refused, and `reason`: `unknown-field`, a field the schema does not name; `missing-required`; `wrong-type`; `not-allowed`, a value of the right type the schema refuses (a constant, a list, a pattern, a bound); or `exactly-one`, one of the ways to say a thing given more than one or none. A runner reads each case against the schema it names, and fails on a verdict, `at` or `reason` other than the case's. A schema with no refused case is held to nothing.",
